<!DOCTYPE html>
<html lang="<%= locale %>">
<head>
    <meta charset="UTF-8">
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0">
    <title><%= __('whitepaper_position_title') %> &bull; KayrosLab</title>
    <script src="https://cdn.tailwindcss.com"></script>
    <link rel="stylesheet" href="https://cdnjs.cloudflare.com/ajax/libs/font-awesome/6.5.1/css/all.min.css">
    <style>@import url('https://fonts.googleapis.com/css2?family=Inter:wght@300;400;500;600&family=Space+Grotesk:wght@500;600&display=swap');body{font-family:'Inter',system-ui,sans-serif;}.font-display{font-family:'Space Grotesk','Inter',sans-serif;}</style>
</head>
<body class="bg-white text-slate-900 antialiased">
    <nav class="bg-white border-b border-slate-200 sticky top-0 z-50">
        <div class="max-w-screen-2xl mx-auto px-5 md:px-8 py-4 flex items-center justify-between">
            <a href="/" class="flex items-center gap-x-2.5">
                <div class="w-9 h-9 bg-slate-900 rounded-xl flex items-center justify-center"><i class="fa-solid fa-brain text-white text-lg"></i></div>
                <span class="font-display text-xl font-semibold tracking-tighter">KayrosLab</span>
            </a>
            <div class="flex items-center gap-x-3">
                <a href="<%= locale === 'en' ? '/index.fr.html' : '/' %>" class="text-xs font-medium px-3 py-1.5 border border-slate-200 rounded-xl hover:bg-slate-50 transition-colors"><%= locale === 'en' ? 'FR' : 'EN' %></a>
                <a href="/" class="text-sm text-slate-600 hover:text-sky-600 transition-colors"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left mr-1"></i> Back to site</a>
            </div>
        </div>
    </nav>

    <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 py-16">
        <div class="mb-8">
            <div class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 px-3 py-1 rounded-full bg-orange-100 text-orange-700 text-xs font-semibold mb-4"><i class="fa-solid fa-file-pdf"></i> <%= __('nav_whitepapers') %></div>
            <h1 class="text-4xl md:text-5xl font-semibold tracking-tighter mb-4"><%= __('whitepaper_position_title') %></h1>
            <p class="text-xl text-slate-600 mb-6"><%= __('whitepaper_position_subtitle') %></p>
        </div>

        <div class="prose prose-slate max-w-none">
            <h2>1. Introduction</h2>
            <p>Positioning an innovation requires a deep understanding of the competitive landscape. Traditional competitive analysis methods are often manual, static and subjective. This white paper presents an ontological approach to competitive analysis that is automated, dynamic and objective.</p>
            
            <h2>2. The Ontological Approach</h2>
            <p>KayrosLab's positioning module uses a 14-type ontology (7 technology entities, 7 business entities) connected by oriented relationships. This formal representation enables precise comparison of competitive offerings across multiple dimensions.</p>
            
            <h2>3. Automated Data Collection</h2>
            <p>The system automatically collects competitive intelligence from multiple sources: web scraping for product and market data, GitHub/GitLab APIs for technology metrics (stars, forks, contributors, commit frequency, freshness, issues), and structured expert input.</p>
            
            <h2>4. Ontology Construction</h2>
            <p>Collected data is structured into the ontology using AI agents (Ontology Designer, Query Engine). Entities are classified, properties are typed, and relationships are oriented to create a rich, queryable knowledge graph.</p>
            
            <h2>5. Gap Analysis</h2>
            <p>The gap analyzer compares your innovation against the competitive landscape, identifying differentiation opportunities, strategic white spaces, and areas of potential competitive threat. Results are visualized in a Cytoscape.js graph with full interactivity.</p>
            
            <h2>6. Export and Reuse</h2>
            <p>The ontology can be exported in OWL RDF/XML format, compliant with the Microsoft Ontology Playground, enabling reuse across your organization and integration with existing knowledge management systems.</p>
            
            <h2>7. Conclusion</h2>
            <p>Ontological competitive analysis transforms positioning from an intuitive art into a rigorous science. By combining automated data collection, formal ontology, and AI-powered analysis, KayrosLab enables organizations to position their innovations with unprecedented precision and objectivity.</p>
        </div>
        
        <div class="mt-12 pt-8 border-t border-slate-200 text-center">
            <a href="/" class="inline-flex items-center gap-x-2 text-sky-600 hover:text-sky-700 font-medium"><i class="fa-solid fa-arrow-left"></i> Back to KayrosLab</a>
        </div>
    </div>

    <footer class="bg-slate-900 text-white py-8">
        <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-8 text-center text-sm text-slate-400">
            <p>&copy; <%= new Date().getFullYear() %> KayrosLab. All rights reserved.</p>
        </div>
    </footer>
</body>
</html>
